    "['unit [unit_number] family [family_type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.10\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n xconnect 1.1.1.1 10 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper \"family ccc\" configuration sets up a circuit cross-connect (CCC) interface\\n- In Cisco, this is equivalent to an MPLS xconnect configuration\\n- The VLAN ID (10) is preserved in the dot1Q encapsulation\\n- The peer address would typically be the router-ID (1.1.1.1 in this case)\\n- The VC ID (10) is arbitrary but should match at both ends of the connection', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation dot1Q 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.10\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n xconnect 1.1.1.1 10 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper \"family ccc\" configuration sets up a circuit cross-connect (CCC) interface\\n- In Cisco, this is equivalent to an MPLS xconnect configuration\\n- The VLAN ID (10) is preserved in the dot1Q encapsulation\\n- The peer address would typically be the router-ID (1.1.1.1 in this case)\\n- The VC ID (10) is arbitrary but should match at both ends of the connection', 'trans_template': 'encapsulation dot1Q 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'xconnect 1.1.1.1 10 encapsulation mpls', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.10\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n xconnect 1.1.1.1 10 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper \"family ccc\" configuration sets up a circuit cross-connect (CCC) interface\\n- In Cisco, this is equivalent to an MPLS xconnect configuration\\n- The VLAN ID (10) is preserved in the dot1Q encapsulation\\n- The peer address would typically be the router-ID (1.1.1.1 in this case)\\n- The VC ID (10) is arbitrary but should match at both ends of the connection', 'trans_template': 'xconnect 1.1.1.1 10 encapsulation mpls'}]]": 1,
